{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_012fc4f7c4358bb86baffaa6b8f41684c2192a294d503728854f43555a4575e1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned GitHub integration would store PRs, comments, links, and sync state in a dedicated SQLite database at ~/.agx/github/prs.sqlite (env-overridable), mirroring the existing Linear adapter pattern; this is planned, not verified as shipped."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6bbcbe2232fc08a532ad3efc1fa8801fb598de1dd55862feb0c927439a7e1c4f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: a GitHub-integration Phase 1 plan instructs agentic workers to use superpowers subagent-driven-development or executing-plans, building schema, stores, OAuth stubs, a link resolver, and sync orchestrator behind an AGX_GITHUB_ENABLED feature flag, TDD-style with Jest and mocked HTTP."}],"claim_ids":["clm_012fc4f7c4358bb86baffaa6b8f41684c2192a294d503728854f43555a4575e1","clm_6bbcbe2232fc08a532ad3efc1fa8801fb598de1dd55862feb0c927439a7e1c4f"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:58Z","created_by_operation":"op_840dc97c38f547d6910760e632ae5d03","id":"pg_84b39112c4325b0480996f56fa40cb7d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/ramarlina-agx-docs-superpowers-plans-2026-04-17-github-integration-pha-6f56fa40cb7d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_625193df09b65913974bbb4b68a35ef1"],"title":"ramarlina/agx/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-17-github-integration-phase1.md @ e674cec11088","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:58Z","updated_by_operation":"op_840dc97c38f547d6910760e632ae5d03"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0baa37ce201822a478a776f7daba1b74abc4ce0f2026dee83d0a4685038640fb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"CLI commands include `agx init` for first-time setup, `agx board start` to open the ticket-agent-PR board, plus project, repo, workspace, and vars subcommands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1d310568b677a06c7fe23d8cfd7116f1c0b0b4e07758110f19a7993dc80db8f7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions are welcomed via GitHub Discussions and Issues, with PRs made by forking main, adding tests, and submitting."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2e847a2d1ace253497f63d58e46dbadc556e402b8ea7e09041811b43c9d26f35"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes provider chat commands such as `agx claude -p`, `agx codex -p`, `agx gemini -p`, and `agx ollama -p`, with single-letter aliases c, x, g, o."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2fc2b97348c1555c5ba81b888cf8c5e7b45f4e70bf58fb5075e95baa03253843"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the repo is an npm workspace with apps/local (Next.js dashboard), apps/desktop (Electron), lib, commands, and cloud-runtime; dev commands include `npm run local:dev`, `local:build`, `board:bundle`, and Electron `build:mac`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3c14424bc4334b88070601ba6dc1305cdcf6292afc9d07318511261da4d86950"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The telemetry documentation states prompts, code, API keys, file paths, and PII are not collected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4dfe9c7a7357fadb0e55e2af544c1074fcb80ba3fdf4394ec3865a5d4e56f005"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents pause for explicit human approve/reject before anything irreversible, and PR review begins with a first pass from a reviewer agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_51026b6e21cca3154de9adb1ae9ccc6e5c97616437ba0732128e603166460e40"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requires Node.js >= 22.16.0 for CLI install and at least one provider CLI (Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, or Ollama); no external database is needed since SQLite is used locally."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69a04ac3a23bf342b9db88c4a08b8fde46a182bea213842d8223a7979d8d1f1b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Telemetry is enabled by default, collecting anonymous usage data such as OS, Node and AGX versions, commands run, provider used, task outcomes, and timing; it can be disabled via `agx telemetry off` or config."},{"claim_ids":["clm_79d0bb44e32584ddb4b06b655ce953583e9282baee7342d263a455a6000b56da"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AGX ships as a CLI, a local web dashboard, and a macOS desktop app from one repository."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8f43a2c17da823b86637cfe0997ec782476659fdd467e501576b100917d2c3dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Work is checkpointed at every step so restarts resume where the user left off, and resuming is described as constant-cost regardless of thread age."},{"claim_ids":["clm_96c4ae598502f6bb42b0056b703d31bc5c276cbf27c518d42cd3a3b7c097e8a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product claims fully local operation with an activity log, signed actions, and destructive-command safeguards."},{"claim_ids":["clm_be95bf4204416c7310220ba674091f41d401029d0aa7d121f6550e2c70bf5d6c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture comprises a SQLite (WAL mode) state layer with durable checkpoints, a CLI plus daemon handling provider tool calls, filesystem edits, and worktree isolation, and a decision layer for human gate transitions and review flow."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0baa37ce201822a478a776f7daba1b74abc4ce0f2026dee83d0a4685038640fb","clm_1d310568b677a06c7fe23d8cfd7116f1c0b0b4e07758110f19a7993dc80db8f7","clm_2e847a2d1ace253497f63d58e46dbadc556e402b8ea7e09041811b43c9d26f35","clm_2fc2b97348c1555c5ba81b888cf8c5e7b45f4e70bf58fb5075e95baa03253843","clm_3c14424bc4334b88070601ba6dc1305cdcf6292afc9d07318511261da4d86950","clm_4dfe9c7a7357fadb0e55e2af544c1074fcb80ba3fdf4394ec3865a5d4e56f005","clm_51026b6e21cca3154de9adb1ae9ccc6e5c97616437ba0732128e603166460e40","clm_69a04ac3a23bf342b9db88c4a08b8fde46a182bea2138